STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    16007                           "Can you tell me how to access a modulator socket?"
    16008                           "Currently, it's not possible. Local data stream functionality is down."
    16009                           "When do you expect the data streams to be back online?"
    16010                           "The bit is missing to get into the control room-otherwise I would reset the data streams myself."
    16013                           "Have you seen a DataWraith yet? Scary."
    16014                           "Some say they're users."
    16015                           "What is a DataWraith?"
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    16016                           "I can't understand a word they're saying. They use a fully encrypted language."
    16017                           "You can always tell when they're coming. Just listen for an eerie clatter."
    16019                           "Both modulators are infested with Resource Hogs."
    16020                           "All it's going to take is for one of those knuckleheads to kick out a power tab and ka-powee! Down goes the socket."
    16029                           "First, I configure the ... no, that's not right. "
    16030                           "Okay ... alright ... okay, first I align the rings then ... then configure them. Not the other way around. Right."
    16031                           "Look at me I'm talking to myself ... "
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    16032                           "New on the job?"
    16033                           "Oh yes. I'm quite nervous."
    16034                           "You'll do just fine. If you don't, the DataWraiths will simply derez you."
    16035                           "Huh?"
    16036                           "First, I align the rings then I configure them. Sounds easy enough."
    16037                           "It occurred to me that they're taking pleasure in my discomfort."
    16038                           "DataWraiths are intimidating, smug and grossly arrogant."
    16039                           "We are so insignificant in their eyes, it's oppressive and belittling. If they are as they claim, I no longer hold Users in high regard."
    16040                           "That seems to be common sentiment amongst us lower level programs."
    16041                           "We are treated like second rate lines of code-disposable and irrelevant."
    16042                           "A frightening reality we are forced to compute."
    16043                           "Hmm, what can one do under the circumstances?"
    16044                           "Are you familiar with the program TRON?"
    16045                           "Yes, of course."
    16046                           "That, my friend, is what one can do. History is repeating itself; we need another hero like TRON."
