STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    4900                            "<color 135 181 255>**Virus Alert** 1@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: **Virus Alert**\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AllPersonnel@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: IT@en.com\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nUnfortunately, not everyone has updated to the new virus protection software and as a result, an unknown virus type has corrupted many systems on Group Seven lab server.\n\nWe're working on the problem right now.\n\nThank you for your patience,\nIT Department"
    4901                            "<color 135 181 255>**Virus Alert** 2@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: **Virus Alert**\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AllPersonnel@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: IT@en.com\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nUntil further notice, do not download or upload files to the central source code server. We are doing our best to quarantine the virus but its aggressive nature is making it extremely difficult. It's really unlike anything we have ever seen before.\n\nSorry for the inconvenience.\nIT Department "
    4902                            "<color 135 181 255> Award Announcement 1@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Award Announcement\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AllPersonal@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Management@en.com\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWe are thrilled to announce that our very own Mr. Alan Bradley has been awarded the highly coveted International Academy of Intelligence Artificielle's 'Digital Pal' award for his latest iteration of Ma3a.\n\nPlease join us and Mr. Bradley in the employee lunch room as we proudly present him the award certificate.\n\nCongratulations Mr. Bradley.\n\nSenior Management"
    4903                            "<color 135 181 255> Award Announcement 2@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Award Announcement\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AllPersonal@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Management@en.com\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIf you see Mr. Bradley, please inform him that he is needed in the employee lunch room.\n\nSenior Management"
    4904                            "<color 135 181 255> Award Announcement 3@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Award Announcement\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AllPersonal@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Management@en.com\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nEvidently, Mr. Bradley is not available to attend the award presentation. For those who are interested, a copy of the award certificate will be featured in the next company newsletter.\n\nSenior Management"
    4905                            "<color 135 181 255> Send me your resume @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Send me your resume\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Jet@house.res<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: AlanBradley@en.com\nDate: Jun-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nLook, son, I know you have a problem with working at the same company as your old man, but I've heard that the Games division is looking for an entry-level programmer. It doesn't pay very well, but it's a foot in the door. Perhaps after a few months you could switch over to R&D.  \n\nAnyway, I won't co-sign for the lease on your new apartment unless you have a job, so I suggest you send in your resume immediately. Don't let pride get in the way of your better judgment.\n\nDad  "
    4906                            "<color 135 181 255> Jethro Bradley @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject:  Jethro Bradley\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AlanBradley@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: HR@en.com\nDate: Jun-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nPer your request I checked our company handbook and there doesn't appear to be any problem with your son working here, nothing in regards to nepotism at least ;). Send his resume over and I'll get it in the system. \n\nMary Jo\nHuman Resources"
    4907                            "<color 135 181 255> Jet 1 @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Jet\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AlanBradley@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Patrick-SP3D@en.com\nDate: Jun-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI got to meet your boy Jet today - a fine young man. He aced the programming test and everyone seems to like him. I didn't see a bit of that 'attitude problem' you keep mentioning. I've got a slot on the Space Paranoids 3D team that's a great fit. \n\nPatrick\nProducer-Space Paranoids 3D"
    4908                            "<color 135 181 255> Jet 2@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Jet\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AlanBradley@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Patrick-SP3D@en.com\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDon't worry, Jet's doing fine. He's more than pulling his weight on the SP3D team; in fact, I'm bumping him up to lead programmer on the next title. There's also a level six programming position opening up in R&D in a few months that would be perfect for him. \n\nPatrick\nProducer-Space Paranoids 3D"
    4909                            "<color 135 181 255> Worried about my job! 1@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Worried about my job!\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Nick@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Olivia@en.com\nDate: Dec-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nBoy, the mood around here is pretty awful. I heard that the CFO is in deep trouble for misallocation of funds. First the Internet bubble burst and now this. I heard that Gibbs Jr. is putting the company up for sale. You know any good headhunters?\n\nOlivia"
    4910                            "<color 135 181 255> Worried about my job! 2@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Worried about my job!\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Olivia@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Nick@en.com\nDate: Dec-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI'm one step ahead of you. I've already sent my resume out to three companies this morning.\n\nA merger is never a pretty sight, especially for the home team. If Gibbs Jr. does indeed sell the company, I bet half of us get laid off. I can't take that chance. I've got two dogs and an expensive car to worry about.\n\nBtw, can I have my stapler back?\n\nNick"
    4911                            "<color 135 181 255> Leaving the Company @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Leaving the Company\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AlanBradley@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: KevinFlynn@en.com\nDate: Jun-90\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWell ol' boy, I'm leaving.\n\nAs you know, this is not a decision I'm making lightly, but the time has come for me move on to greener pastures. Gibbs Jr. will take over operations.\n\nMy days here since replacing Dillinger have been both fulfilling and heart breaking, I'll never forget the great moments we've shared.\n\nCome by my office early tonight and well have a drink.\n\nKevin Flynn\nSenior Executive V.P."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    4912                            "<color 135 181 255> Acquisition 1@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Acquisition\nTo: <color 255 255 0>GibbsJr@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: CEO@fCon.ind\nDate: Dec-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nA courier should be arriving shortly to deliver my final proposal. I hope you find the terms of the deal acceptable and in order.\n\nThe merging of our two companies will lay the groundwork for a brighter future for all of us. Please consider this as a new beginning and not as a failure on your part.\n\nCEO\nFuture Control Industries"
    4913                            "<color 135 181 255> Acquisition 2@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject:  Acquisition\nTo: <color 255 255 0> CEO@fCon.ind<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: GibbsJr@en.net\nDate: Dec-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI think we agree on the main points. I'll have my lawyer start on the contract tomorrow. \n\nGibbs Jr.\nSenior Executive V.P."
    4914                            "<color 135 181 255> Acquisition 3@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Acquisition\nTo: <color 255 255 0>GibbsJr@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: AlanBradley@en.com\nDate: Dec-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI don't mean any disrespect, but I've been with the company for over 20 years and I don't think your father would have been happy with the current state of affairs. Please reconsider selling the company - sure, the economy is in a bad state, but I think that we've got some promising new technologies that will restore the company to its former glory (once we've worked out the bugs, of course).\n\nAlan Bradley\nSenior Programming Engineer"
    4915                            "<color 135 181 255> Acquisition 4@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject:  Acquisition\nTo:  <color 255 255 0>CEO@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: ExecVP@en.com\nDate: Dec-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI can't tell you how terrible I feel about the current position of the company. I take full responsibility. Unfortunately, selling is the only viable option considering the circumstances. I feel extremely fortunate that fCon is so eager to buy our company and is willing to pay the price we put on the table. \n\nPlease understand that this is something I must do.\n\nGibbs Jr.\nSenior Executive V.P."
    4916                            "<color 135 181 255> Digitizing Technology 1@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject:  Digitizing Technology\nTo: <color 255 255 0>GibbsJr@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: LoraBradley@fCon.ind\nDate: Feb-84\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWe noticed random fluctuations during the digital conversion experiments that will need to be corrected somehow. The MCP's unique ability to 'learn' enabled it to perform computations beyond current science. Without it, I'm afraid it may be years before we re-establish the ability to digitize matter correctly.\n\nThe only thing I can think of is perhaps a set of algorithms that can be written to compensate for these fluctuations. The complexity of these algorithms is quite frankly unfathomable, but I believe it is theoretically possible.\n\nLora Bradley\nProgramming Engineer"
    4917                            "<color 135 181 255> Digitizing Technology 2@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject:  Digitizing Technology\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AllPersonal@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Management@en.com\nDate: Oct-94\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nAs many of you have already heard, there was a serious accident in the lab yesterday involving Lora Bradley.\n\nUntil the investigations into the cause of the misfiring laser are complete, the digitizing lab is temporarily off limits to all employees.\n\nSenior Management"
    4918                            "<color 135 181 255> Digitizing Technology 3@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject:  Digitizing Technology\nTo:  <color 255 255 0>GibbsJr@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: AlanBradley@en.com\nDate: Aug-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWe've finally made a breakthrough in our digitization technology, although it is far from perfect. The 'analog-to-digital conversion' is functional and we are nearly complete with the necessary algorithms. Ma3a and I should have them done in the next few months.\n\nIt's been a long road but we are almost there. Lora was right about the algorithms. I wish she was here to celebrate this moment.\n\nAlan Bradley\nSenior Programming Engineer"
    4919                            "<color 135 181 255> Tron Legacy Code 1@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Tron Legacy Code\nTo: <color 255 255 0>KevinFlynn@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: AlanBradley@en.com\nDate: Aug-84\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI'm a little confused. I noticed that the Tron Legacy code upgrade is no longer listed on the fourth quarter schedule. Is there something I should know?\n\nAlan Bradley\nSenior Programming Engineer"
    4920                            "<color 135 181 255> Tron Legacy Code 2@------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Tron Legacy Code\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AlanBradley@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: KevinFlynn@en.com\nDate: Aug-84\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSorry Alan, I'm pulling the plug on the Tron Legacy project. I know, I know-I requested the upgrade but as you know, research in digitization is behind schedule. In fact, destroying the Master Control Program has set us back to the stone age.\n\nAnyway, the Board of Directors wants our top programmers moved to the project and you, my friend, are one of the best. Report to Walter on Monday.\n\nI realize shelving Tron hurts, but look at it this way; you'll be working side by side with your lovely wife. \n\nKevin Flynn\nSenior Executive V.P."
    4921                            "<color 135 181 255> Tron Legacy Code 3@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Tron Legacy Code\nTo: <color 255 255 0>KevinFlynn@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: AlanBradley@en.com\nDate: Aug-84\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nAs much as I hate the idea of putting a project half complete to the side, I can't deny the logic behind your decision. Tron Legacy is unnecessary if we are not able to digitize anything in the first place.\n \nI'm putting the source code and the latest build notes on our dedicated memory mainframe, EN12-82.\n\nAlan Bradley\nSenior Programming Engineer\n\nPS: Oh, and yes, working with Lora should be great fun."
    4922                            "<color 135 181 255> Lost and Found @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Lost and Found\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AlanBradley@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: SergeantDawson@police.co\nDate: Mar-98\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGood Afternoon Mr. Bradley,\n\nDuring your visit with us yesterday, you must have inadvertently left your wallet on the counter while filling out Jet's release forms. The cleaning service turned it in last night. You are welcome to come by at your earliest convenience to reclaim your property.\n\nThank you,\nSergeant T. Dawson"
    4923                            "<color 135 181 255> Trouble at School @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Trouble at School\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AlanBradley@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Bond@ValleyHS.dep\nDate: Mar-98\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGood day Mr. Bradley,\n\nI have received several reports from the faculty here at Valley High concerning Jet's despondent behavior during class. His flippant responses are often disruptive and his lack of respect toward his teachers is terribly inappropriate.\n\nJet is a good boy and quite smart. However, as principal, I must request a conference with you in hopes to resolve this potentially destructive path he is currently on.\n\nCan you make Tuesday at 5:30?\n\nThank you,\nMr. Bond\nPrincipal"
    4924                            "<color 135 181 255> Home Late @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Home Late\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AlanBradley@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Jet@house.res\nDate: Aug-98\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGoing over to a friend's house.\n\nBe home ... some time.\n\nJ."
    4925                            "<color 135 181 255> Your Grades @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Your Grades\nTo: <color 255 255 0>JetBradley@university.edu <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: AlanBradley@en.com \nDate: Feb-99\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nJet:\n\nI was disappointed when I saw your report card - A's in your comp sci classes don't make up for three incompletes.  \n\nI wanted to talk to you about this in person but you never seem to be home.\n\nCall me at work.\n\nDad"
    4926                            "<color 135 181 255> How are you holding up?@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: How are you holding up?\nTo: <color 255 255 0>KFlynn@anotheremail.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: AlanBradley@en.com\nDate: Oct-99\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSo glad to hear from you, old friend.\n\nThere's no need to worry about me, I've gotten on pretty well since the passing of Lora. It's Jet that I'm worried about. A real handful he's been!\n\nWhat are you up to these days? Are you still considering pitching your experience in the computer world to Hollywood? Hmm, I wonder who would play my part? Someone handsome, I hope :)\n\nAnyway, thanks for the email and don't be such a stranger.\n\nAlan Bradley\nSenior Programming Engineer"
    4927                            "<color 135 181 255> Company Merge @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Company Merge\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AllPersonal@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Management@en.com\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nLoyalty, hard work and talent. All hallmarks of our company for so many years. Unfortunately, times have been tough and no longer are we able to continue relying on these merits alone. Merging with fCon is necessary if we are to survive the future economy.\n\nAs of today, fCon will be taking over the day-to-day operations. Please remain at your workstations and await further instruction from an fCon representative.\n\nThank You,\nSenior Management"
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    4928                            "<color 135 181 255> Team Portfolio @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Team Portfolio\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Management@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: CEO@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nEffective immediately, all senior managers are to report directly to the following fCon representatives.\n\nSeth Crown III, Attorney\nCorporate Attorney\nCrown@fCon.ind\n\nDr. Eva Popoff, Ph.D.\nCorporate Human Resources\nPopoff@fCon.ind\n\nEsmond Baza, M.S.\nCorporate Technician\nBaza@fCon.ind\n\nCEO\nFuture Control Industries, Inc."
    4929                            "<color 135 181 255> Simulator Online @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Simulator Online\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Crown@fCon.ind<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Baza@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nAs promised, the DataWraith training simulator is ready for testing. \n\nEsmond Baza\nChief Technology Officer\nFuture Control Industries, Inc."
    4930                            "<color 135 181 255> Seth Crown III @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n<color 255 255 0>Subject: Seth Crown III<color 135 181 255>\nCorporate Attorney\nFuture Control Industries\nDate: Jan-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n<color 255 255 255>Born:\n<color 135 181 255>9-25-74\n<color 255 255 255>Place of Birth:\n<color 135 181 255>New York, New York, USA\n<color 255 255 255>Education:\n<color 135 181 255>Harvard University\nCambridge, Massachusetts\n<color 255 255 255>Comments:\n<color 135 181 255>A Natural leader. Very rarely shows his emotions making it difficult to judge his sincerity and true motives."
    4931                            "<color 135 181 255> Dr. Eva Popoff @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n<color 255 255 0>Subject: Dr. Eva Popoff<color 135 181 255>\nCorporate Human Resources\nFuture Control Industries\nDate: Jan-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n<color 255 255 255>Born:\n<color 135 181 255>3-13-78\n<color 255 255 255>Place of Birth:\n<color 135 181 255>Lyon, France\n<color 255 255 255>Education:\n<color 135 181 255>American University of Paris\nParis, France\n<color 255 255 255>Comments:\n<color 135 181 255>A very driven individual. Speaks fluent English as well as German, Russian and Cantonese. Excellent at managing large groups of people but somewhat unapproachable in one on one situations."
    4932                            "<color 135 181 255> Esmond Baza @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n<color 255 255 0>Subject: Esmond Baza<color 135 181 255>\nChief Technology Officer\nFuture Control Industries\nDate: Jan-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n<color 255 255 255>Born:\n<color 135 181 255>11-10-71\n<color 255 255 255>Place of Birth:\n<color 135 181 255>Delhi, India\n<color 255 255 255>Education:\n<color 135 181 255>University of Leicester\nLeicester England\n<color 255 255 255>Comments:\n<color 135 181 255>Graduated Summa Cum Laude. Esmond is extremely self-critical. He often fails to recognize his own achievements, leading to frequent bouts of severe depression."
    4933                            "<color 135 181 255> DataWraith Training @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: DataWraith Training (transcript)\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Crown@fCon.ind<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Popoff@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMr. Crown,\nGood news!\n\nWe've completed the first phase of training. Our DataWraiths are adapting well to the environmental simulators. The biological stress appears to be minimal.\n\nThe real test now is to see how effective they are against various types of security protocol measures. \n\nShould be interesting.\n\nDr. Eva Popoff, Ph.D.\nCorporate Human Resources\nFuture Control Industries"
    4934                            "<color 135 181 255> Executive Update @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Executive Update\nTo: <color 255 255 0>CEO@fCon.ind <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Popoff@fCon.ind\nDate:Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nHere's the update you requested--\n\nWe have trained hundreds of hand picked associates operating under the moniker DataWraiths. Their objective is to gather information quickly and quietly from inside the digital universe. \n\nNo scrap of data will be private from our DataWraiths!\n\nPIN numbers, passwords, emails will be at our disposal and with this information; fCon can exert unprecedented influence on peoples and nations. In fact, we may even go as far as erasing any of those who oppose us!\n\nDr. Eva Popoff\nDirector, Human Resources\nFuture Control Industries, Inc."
    4935                            "<color 135 181 255> Correction Algorithms 1@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Correction algorithms\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Baza@fCon.ind<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Crown@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI paid our Guest another visit. After a few persuasive threats, I managed to learn the location of the correction algorithms.\n\nMeet me outside storage room 'B' in ten and I'll fill you in. I want to get our programmers on it right away!\n\nSeth Crown III, Attorney\nCorporate Attorney\nFuture Control Industries"
    4936                            "<color 135 181 255> JD Thorne 1@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: JD Thorne\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Crown@fCon.ind<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Popoff@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nMany employees are starting to question the whereabouts of our Mr. Thorne. His position as Security Chief carries a rather high profile. We need to address the issue soon.\n\nLet's discuss in the next team meeting.\n\nDr. Eva Popoff, Ph.D.\nCorporate Human Resources\nFuture Control Industries"
    4937                            "<color 135 181 255> JD Thorne 2@----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: JD Thorne\nTo: <color 255 255 0> Popoff@fCon.ind<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Crown@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI suggest we simply inform Thorne's co-workers that he is out sick with a REALLY bad virus :)\n\nSeth Crown III, Attorney\nCorporate Attorney\nFuture Control Industries"
    4938                            "<color 135 181 255> Correction algorithms 2@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Correction algorithms\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Crown@fCon.ind<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Baza@fCon.ind \nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWe've completed the modifications to our Seeker engine per our earlier conversation. It should locate our target in no time. \n\nI'll keep you posted.\n\nEsmond Baza, M.S.\nCorporate Technician\nFuture Control Industries"
    4939                            "<color 135 181 255> Tron Arcade Game @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Tron Arcade Game\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AlanBradley@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: KevinFlynn@en.com\nDate: Feb-82\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI have another video arcade game idea - mind if I use the name of your security program? Promise I'll give you credit. Thanks in advance.\n\nKevin Flynn\nSenior Executive V.P."
    4940                            "<color 135 181 255> Hypothetical Situation 1@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Hypothetical Situation\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AlanBradley@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: KevinFlynn@en.com \nDate: Oct-83\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI'm terribly concerned about the possibility of our digitizing technology (if we can get it working again) falling into the wrong hands. \n\nJust think about it. A User free to exist in the computer realm unchecked-it's a scary thought! \n\nIt's a contingency we must prepare for, because I'll tell ya, I'm starting to lose sleep over it.\n\nWhat are your thoughts on this?\n\nKevin Flynn\nSenior Executive V.P."
    4941                            "<color 135 181 255> Hypothetical Situation 2@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Hypothetical Situation\nTo: <color 255 255 0> KevinFlynn@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: AlanBradley@en.com \nDate: Oct-83\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nMan free to manipulate the computer from the inside. That is indeed a very unsettling scenario.\n\nI must admit that it's a little difficult for me to comprehend exactly the experience you had in the computer, but based on your account, your concerns are certainly justified.\n\nThe first thing that comes to mind is Tron. Possibly an upgrade to expand the program's base properties to include the monitoring of unauthorized User activity.\n\nI'll put together some projections.\n\nAlan Bradley\nSenior Programming Engineer"
    4942                            "<color 135 181 255> Tron Upgrade @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Tron Upgrade\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AlanBradley@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: KevinFlynn@en.com \nDate: Oct-83\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nLet's move ahead on the Tron Upgrade project as we discussed.\n\nKevin Flynn\nSenior Executive V.P."
    4943                            "<color 135 181 255> Tron Upgrade Status @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Tron Upgrade Status\nTo: <color 255 255 0>KevinFlynn@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: AlanBradley@en.com \nDate: Dec-83\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFlynn,\nI've got the new Tron update up and running but it's far from being ready.\n\nIt's impossible to actually verify, but my calculations indicate that my Tron update is unable to discern between authorized Users and Users gone rogue. \n\nIt's a bug I'm trying to iron out. So far it's been a real stumper.\n\nAlan Bradley\nSenior Programming Engineer"
END

