STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    4944                            "<color 135 181 255> New Parents @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: New Parents\nTo: <color 255 255 0> LoraBradley@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: KevinFlynn@en.com\nDate: May-82\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWell, this is wonderful news!\n\nYou two didn't waste much time, did you?\n\nI would be honored to be the youngster's Godfather.\n\nKevin Flynn\nSenior Executive V.P."
    4945                            "<color 135 181 255> It's a boy!@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: It's a boy!\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AllPersonal@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: KevinFlynn@en.com\nDate: Dec-82\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDear Employees,\n\nI'm happy to announce the arrival of Jethro Eugene Bradley. \n\nJethro weighs in at a modest 7lbs 8oz, with blue eyes and brown hair.\n\nI fully expect him to tackle Space Paranoid's level twelve bonus area within a few months, that is, if he's anything like his ol' Godfather Flynn!\n\nProud parents and new baby are healthy and currently home resting after a very exciting two days.\n\nWe wish them the very best.\n\nKevin Flynn\nSenior Executive V.P."
    4946                            "<color 135 181 255> Lab AI Development 1@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Lab AI Development\nTo: <color 255 255 0>KevinFlynn@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: AlanBradley@en.com\nDate: Jan-88\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI believe Lora and I have discovered a new logic matrix that will produce a 1213% increase in simple numerical computation as well as simulated reasoning.\n\nWe're hoping to complete a prototype early this spring.\n\nLora is currently calling the artificial intelligence, Math Assistant One. I don't know if the name will stick. Only time will tell.\n\nAlan Bradley\nSenior Programming Engineer"
    4947                            "<color 135 181 255> Lab AI Development 2@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Lab AI Development\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AlanBradley@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: KevinFlynn@en.com\nDate: Jan-88\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nNothing like a glorified calculator to help dull the mind!\n\nAre we looking at a marketable product or is Math Assistant One strictly intended for internal use only?\n\nThe company could sure use a shot in the arm. A new source of revenue would be a welcome addition, considering our current expenditures trying to reclaim our lost technology in digitization.\n\nBtw, will this new assistant of yours fetch coffee?\n\nKevin Flynn\nSenior Executive V.P."
    4948                            "<color 135 181 255> Lab AI Development 3@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Lab AI Development\nTo: <color 255 255 0>KevinFlynn@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: AlanBradley@en.com\nDate: Mar-88\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI apologize for having to postpone the presentation. Lora discovered a rather significant memory leak in Math Assistant One's new Voice recognition subprograms. The good news is, Math Assistant One Audio or Ma1a as we now call it, now recognizes over sixty four common verbal commands without crashing the vocoder buffer.\n\nMa1a should prove to be a useful companion in many research laboratory applications.\n\nPlease inform the Board that I do plan on making the 2pm presentation scheduled tomorrow.\n\nAlan Bradley\nSenior Programming Engineer"
    4949                            "<color 135 181 255> Creepy!!!@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Creepy!!!\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Gabrielle@en.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Meghan@en.com\nDate: Jun-96\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nCreepy isn't the half of it! \n\nWhen Mr. Bradley upgraded Ma1a to Ma2a, which was only about a year ago, many felt the AI exhibited personality traits of his dead wife.\n\nTake the voice, for example. Some say it's simply a digital recreation of Mrs. Bradley's voice, others speculate she recorded a vast word library from her death bed. There's even a rumor that she was partially digitized during the laser accident and Alan managed to salvage the DNA and integrate it into the AI.\n\nReal science fiction stuff if you ask me. I wouldn't pay too much attention to the rumors.\n\nMeghan"
    4950                            "<color 135 181 255> Something Fishy about fCon @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Something Fishy about fCon\nTo: <color 255 255 0>KevinFlynn@anotheremail.com <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: AlanBradley@en.com\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI don't know if you use this email address anymore, but I thought I'd give it a try. Junior has convinced the board to sell the company to fCon. What I've heard of them, I don't like. The irony is that Ma3a has finally computed the correction algorithms that are the final piece of the puzzle. We've come full circle. Unfortunately, my conscience won't allow me to tell my future employers of this discovery. I've embedded the algorithms in Ma3a's code base but they're encrypted so even if someone had access to her source code they'd have a tough time figuring it out.\n\nAlan Bradley\nSenior Programming Engineer"
    4951                            "<color 135 181 255> Correction Algorithms 1@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Correction Algorithms\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Crown@fCon.ind <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Baza@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI'm having difficulties extracting the correction algorithms from the Ma3a code base. The time required will exceed our launch window.\n\nHow shall I proceed?\n\nOn a side note, the amount of legacy code in Ma3a is rather extensive. I'm surprised Alan would compile such a mess.\n\nEsmond Baza, M.S.\nCorporate Technician\nFuture Control Industries"
    4952                            "<color 135 181 255> Correction Algorithms 2@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Correction Algorithms\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Baza@fCon.ind <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Crown@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe scheduled launch is not flexible. Do what must be done to get the correction algorithms installed-and working!\n\nSeth Crown III, Attorney\nCorporate Attorney\nFuture Control Industries"
    4953                            "<color 135 181 255> Correction Algorithms 3@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Correction Algorithms\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Crown@fCon.ind <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Baza@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI've come up with a solution. I've installed the AI and linked the correction algorithms to the digitizing system much like the method used in his lab. It's a little unstable at the moment due to all the legacy code, but I'll have it shored up in no time. \n\nEsmond Baza, M.S.\nCorporate Technician\nFuture Control Industries"
    4954                            "<color 135 181 255> Alan Bradley @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Alan Bradley\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Crown@fCon.ind <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Baza@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nApparently, our boy was busy during his little stay in the storeroom.\n\nHe managed to configure an old game console and a terribly ancient modem to connect to the network. There is no way of knowing whom he communicated with-if the contraption worked at all! \n\nJust another loose end to worry about.\n\nEsmond Baza, M.S.\nCorporate Technician\nFuture Control Industries"
    4955                            "<color 135 181 255> Proposition @<color 191 255 0>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Prop^osition\nTo: <color 255 255 0>JD#Thorne@en.com<color 191 255 0>\nFrom: CEO@fCon.ind\nDate: Dec-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFuture Control Industries is very <>#*^(* interested in contracting your services. I would like to set up a meeting to discuss a partnership in more detail.\n\nPlease con#tact my sec&etary. \n\nL&oking 3y@&^*forward to meetin(g you Mr. Thorne.\n\nCEO\nFuture Control@#(*& Industries"
    4956                            "<color 135 181 255> Welcome to the Team @<color 191 255 0>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Welc&ome to the Team\nTo: <color 255 255 0>JDTh7orne@en.com<color 191 255 0>\nFrom: Crown@fCon.ind\nDate: Dec-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMr. Tho@^rne,   \nGlad to have you on board. \n\nWe're*#&( on the brin*k of a new digital world order. What we do in the course of the next few months, may shift the structure of government ^#)^@and military power, as we know it.\n\nBut first we ne@ed to acquire)(#*)# the Digit#ization technology, and that Mr. Thorne, is where you come in. As Chief of Security, you ar>e in a unique position to gain access to technologies required to s^et our plan in motion. \n\nI'll be pers)(onally overseeing your progr&ess. %^#*# Report to me directly of your findings.\n\nSeth Crown III, Attorney\nCorp#orate Attorney\nFuture Co&ntrol Industries"
    4957                            "<color 135 181 255> New Chair 1@<color 191 255 0>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: N@ew Chair\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Valentine6554@en.com<color 191 255 0> \nFrom: Ala#nBradley@en.com\nDate: Sept 02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMs. Valentine, \n\nAs of today, I'm()#*&(*&@# still not in receipt of my new chair I order##ed over three weeks ago.\n\nI'm n#ormally (*@&(#HBE(not pushy like this, but(#*&( I'm experien*cing extreme back pain sitting in my current chair.\n\nC%an you please look into the mat#(*(*Y#@ter and possibly expedite the delivery if possible?\n\nThank you,\n\nAlan Bra#(*dley\nSenior Programm^%ing Engineer"
    4958                            "<color 135 181 255> New Chair 2@<color 191 255 0>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: New Ch#(air\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AlanBr()*#Jadley@en.com<color 191 255 0> \nFrom: V#alentine6554@en.com\nDate: Sept 02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe invoice num#(*ber shows the chair #(&#_#_)#)N(was delivered Thursday of last week. It wasn't en#)*(U&tirely clear who it was for, so I #)*098#)gave it to Carol in acc)*()(#ounting.\n\nDeb Valentine\nAssi)#*(&tant Office Manager"
    4959                            "<color 135 181 255> Prescription @<color 191 255 0>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Pres(*cription\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Ala@nBradley@en.com<color 191 255 0> \nFro*&m: ValleyDrug@business.biz\nDate: Nov 02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMr. Br**#N(()@@adley\n\nYour presc_(&*#iption medication for lower b)#M(ii#back pain is ready.\n\nWe clo)#(M#se at 6:00 pm tonight._0,_#(,90\n\nValley #Drug\nProviding )#Mcertified pharmaceutical care for twenty-five years."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    4960                            "<color 135 181 255> Digitizing is Possible 1@<color 191 255 0>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Digi%tizing is Possible\nTo: <color 255 255 0>CEO@fCon.ind<color 191 255 0> \nFrom: Cr*own@fCon.ind\nDate: N()*@&ov-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nAccor$&ding to Th*orne, Bradley has done the impossible. Thorne saw Bradley shoot a laser beam at an orange. The orange disap$&peared under the beam, and th*&#*@en reappeared intact a few sec)($onds later. He's posting the su*9rveillance video to my private ftp site - I'll let you know when to dow($*nload it.\n\nSeth Crown III, Atto)),rney\nCorporate Attorney\nFuture C&ontrol Industries, Inc."
    4961                            "<color 135 181 255> Digitizing is Possible 2@<color 191 255 0>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Digitizing is Pos@sible\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Crown@fCon.ind <color 191 255 0>\nFrom: CEO@fCon.ind\nDate: Nov-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWell d(@one, Mr. Crown.\n\nAs you kn@)(ow I've had my eye on this company for quite s#)ome time. Tell our new friend that we'd be willing to kee#)(%^p up our end of the bargain when we have proof. In the mea,ntime, you can put him on the payroll as a freelan(^#Kce consultant.\n\nCEO\nFuture Con!trol Industries, Inc."
    4962                            "<color 135 181 255> Nothing but a smoke screen!@<color 191 255 0>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Nothing but a smoke screen!\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Crown@fCon.ind<color 191 255 0> \nFrom: JDThorne@en.com\nDate: Dec-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI've been po)($.king my nose around the labs concerning these Correction algo*&@!rithms. I personally feel it's a bunch of po$*<litical gibberish in*$itiated by Mr. Bradley to help sustain the generous a><mount of funding that goes into his department.\n\nThe Correcti#(on algorithms are nothing mo)re than a smoke screen. T)!(@here is no reason to delay the scheduled test run.\n\nJ.D. Tho3rne\nChief of Se*(&^curity"
    4963                            "<color 135 181 255> Promotion @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Promotion\nTo: <color 255 255 0>JDThorne@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: HR@en.com\nDate: May-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI'm sorry to tell you that the Board of Directors has decided not to promote you to Vice President of Corporate Security. Mr. Gibbs apologizes for not telling you in person but as you know he's away on business in Asia right now.\n\nMary Jo\nHuman Resources"
    4964                            "<color 135 181 255> Freelance Work @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Freelance Work\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Crown@fCon.ind<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: JDThorne@en.com\nDate: Jul-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nA mutual friend has suggested that I contact you regarding possible freelance work. While I am currently Director of Corporate Security for ENCOM, my contract allows me to take on freelance work. I look forward to hearing from you.\n\nJ.D. Thorne\nChief of Security"
    4965                            "<color 135 181 255> Freelance Work 2@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Freelance Work\nTo: <color 255 255 0>JDThorne@en.com<color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Crown@fCon.ind\nDate: Jul-02\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFuture Control Industries is very interested in contracting your services. I would like to set up a meeting to discuss a partnership in more detail.\n\nPlease contact my secretary. \n\nLooking forward to meeting you Mr. Thorne.\n\nSeth Crown III, Attorney\nCorporate Attorney\nFuture Control Industries, Inc."
    4966                            "<color 135 181 255> Digitization Progress @-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Digitization Progress\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Crown@fCon.ind <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Popoff@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWe have just completed digitizing the first wave of DataWraiths. There were a few bugs initially, but the process is currently working as expected. Proceeding on schedule.\n\nWe did it!\n\nDr. Eva Popoff, Ph.D.\nCorporate Human Resources\nFuture Control Industries"
    4967                            "<color 135 181 255> Security Update 1@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Security Update\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Crown@fCon.ind <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Baza@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nHere's the update you requested.\n\nWe've completed the installation of the latest in firewall technology. There's no way our network will have a breach of security, I'll bet my good-looks on it :)\n\nAnyway, on a more serious note, I detected some activity through our wireless connection which is not, let me say this again, IS NOT routed through our new firewall.\n\nIt was probably just a surge anomaly but for security sake, I suggest we terminate that account ASAP. It could haunt us later down the road.\n\nEsmond Baza, M.S.\nCorporate Technician\nFuture Control Industries"
    4968                            "<color 135 181 255> Security Update 2@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Security Update\nTo: <color 255 255 0> Baza@fCon.ind <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Crown@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe only account still open is registered to that idiot we hired, J.D. Thorne. \n\nMr. Baza shut it down immediately and send a team down to Thorne's office right away. I want all computer drives erased. Also retrieve all electrical devices that may contain incriminating evidence (e.g. cell phone, PDA, etc.)\n\nSeth Crown III, Attorney\nCorporate Attorney\nFuture Control Industries, Inc."
    4969                            "<color 135 181 255> Server Launch Schedule 1@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Server Launch Schedule\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Baza@fCon.ind <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: LabTech@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nAll system components have been installed and debugged. The Server can be brought online at your request.\n\nLabTech\nFuture Control Industries"
    4970                            "<color 135 181 255> Server Launch Schedule 2@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Server Launch Schedule\nTo: <color 255 255 0>LabTech@fCon.ind <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Baza@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGood, I'll pass the news along to the team. \n\nBegin launch sequence. I want this thing up and running and fully loaded with DataWraiths ASAP. Scheduled transfer onto the Net is still green.\n\nWhat's the status on the transmission tools?\n\nEsmond Baza, M.S.\nCorporate Technician\nFuture Control Industries"
    4971                            "<color 135 181 255> Server Launch Schedule 3@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Server Launch Schedule\nTo: <color 255 255 0>Crown@fCon.ind <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: Baza@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nOur engineers are currently conducting their final tests on our proprietary file transferring technology. I don't foresee any delays.\n\nEsmond Baza, M.S.\nCorporate Technician\nFuture Control Industries"
    4972                            "<color 135 181 255> Congratulations!@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Congratulations!\nTo: <color 255 255 0>AllPersonal@fCon.ind <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: CEO@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nAs we near our launch I want to take this time to congratulate the team on a job well done. Soon, all the long hours and hard work will pay off.\n\nWe are the beginning of a new influence. A new Adam and Eve if you will. We will have the ability to sway the masses' perception of what is right and what is wrong. We will create a world according to our terms.\n\nBe proud of your accomplishments and look forward to a new kind of future!\n\nCEO\nFurture Control Industries"
    4973                            "<color 135 181 255> Report 1@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Report\nTo: <color 255 255 0>LabTech@fCon.ind <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: CEO@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI want a report explaining what happened to Mr. Crown, Mr. Baza and Ms Popoff emailed to me in ten minutes!\n\nI've been waiting twenty years for this moment. I don't want this company to slip through my fingers again.\n\nCEO\nFurture Control Industries"
    4974                            "<color 135 181 255> Report 2@-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSubject: Report\nTo: <color 255 255 0>CEO@fCon.ind <color 135 181 255>\nFrom: LabTech@fCon.ind\nDate: Mar-03\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nUnfortunately, Mr. Crown, Mr. Baza and Ms Popoff have been digitized into the system without the correction algorithms.\n\nThe algorithms were extracted from Ma3a the moment we digitized the team in. I'm afraid there is nothing I can do to save them. If I were to bring them back now, I'm pretty sure they wouldn't return ... well, as they were.\n \nLabTech\nFuture Control Industries"
END

