STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10656              "Warning. Core settings exceed default specifications."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10657              "Power modulation unstable."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10658              "We've got activity here. The port is going live."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10659              "That must be Ma3a. I'll be right there."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10660              "Stranger, there is something I want to ask you."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10661              "The future-are there programs ... like me?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10662              "What do you mean?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10663              "You know, programs from my era."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10664              "I'm sorry ... "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10665              "That's okay ... I know ... "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10666              "Have you found the TRON Legacy code yet?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10667              "No, but I've met an old program who seems to know everything about this system."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10668              "Ma3a, this is I-No. I-No, Ma3a."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10669              "What a configuration ... "
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10673              "I-No found the directory containing the TRON Legacy code."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10674              "Meet us in the lower disc partition. There are two primary pipelines from your location. Unfortunately, both are heavily populated with resource hogs. Good luck, stranger."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10675              "Hurry, Jet! We'll be waiting for you."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10676              "Ma3a ... (garbled) ... status?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10677              "Guest!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10678              "My name is Jet Bradley. Contact my father, Alan Bradley, and tell him I'm in the computer-I know it sounds crazy, but it's an emergency!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10679              "Jet ... (garbled) ... how the heck! ... (garbled) ... do not ... (garbled)"
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10688              "Come with us, I-No."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10689              "I can't, stranger. There's no place in the future for an old program like me. I'd be swallowed up and derezzed before I could spit out my first routine."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10690              "This place ... there's not much time left."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10691              "Yes ... but it's my home. A place that I know."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10692              "All right.  Thanks for your help, I-No. I won't forget you."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10693              "See that you don't."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10694              "Ma3a, where are we going?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10695              "The Net."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10696              "This place is enormous."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10697              "The Net is made up of thousands of hubs like this. Data and programs of every type imaginable pass through here."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10699              "But that's why we're here.  This is the best place to find a compiler program, right?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10700              "Precisely!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10703              "Okay, I'll find us a way to compile the TRON Legacy code."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10704              "Pssst! You want a subroutine?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10708              "I got a beta version of the latest viral mesh protection. It's perfect for protecting your code against the corruption."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10711              "Where did you get it?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10712              "That's not important."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10713              "Okay, sounds like a good deal, I'll take it."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10716              "Here ya go."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10795              "Mercury!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10796              "Identity verification."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10797              "Mercury, it's me, Jet. Don't you recognize me?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10798              "My User needs to communicate with you."
