    IDS_DIALOGUE_10889              "Going somewhere?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10892              "Uh ... "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10893              "I'm not falling for that old trick, User."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10894              "No ... I'm not finished."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10895              "I found Ma3a! Saving to disk now."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10896              "Sir, once Alan revealed the location of the correction algorithms, it was only a matter of time before our Seeker engine found Ma3a."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10897              "Good work, Mr. Crown. Now we can correct the digitization process so there won't be any more mistakes like Thorne."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10898              "Go to Phase Two."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10900              "Dad? Is it you?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10901              "Jet ... (garbled) ... safe ... (garbled) ... Ma3a?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10902              "What's wrong with your connection?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10903              " ... (garbled) ... locked ... (garbled) ... storage room ... (garbled)... accessing the ... (garbled) ... with ... (garbled) ... game console. It's the best ... (garbled) ... under ... (garbled) ... circumstances."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10904              "Can you get me out of here?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10905              "Not without Ma3a ... (garbled) ... algorithms."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10906              " ... (garbled) ... losing my connection. ... (garbled) ... sending a back ... (garbled) ... copy of Mercury ... (garbled) ... help ... (garbled) ..."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10914              "Attention! All programs quit current actions. This access node is offline and restricted. Illegal use of resources is punishable by immediate deresolution."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10916              "I've been instructed to aid you in freeing my User."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10917              "I will configure the exit port. However, you must remove the security clamp from the array modulator before this can be done."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10918              "Mercury, do you not recognize me at all?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10919              "Do you understand these instructions?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10920              "Yes but ... "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10921              "Routing configuration complete. Enter the exit port."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10922              "Where am I going? And what about you, Mercury?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10923              "I am not instructed to follow. My command buffer is empty."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10924              "I don't understand how is this going to help my Dad."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10925              "Unable to process your query."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10927              "I hope this works."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10932              "What are you doing?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10933              "Before we digitize any DataWraiths, I want to make sure the correction algorithms fix the problem."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10934              "Dad, get out of there!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10935              "Ah, thank you Mr. Bradley, you just solved a small problem for us."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10936              "If he survives, our DataWraiths can hunt him down. "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10937              "This will never work."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10938              "Mr. Baza, please lead our distinguished guest to the digitization pad."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10939              "You should be ecstatic, Mr. Bradley. You are about to taste the fruit of all your hard work. Savor it while you can."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10942              "What is this place?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10943              "There you are. I've been worried."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10944              "Son, I'm okay. "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10945              "Where are you? What did they do to you?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10946              "I'm here! I'm actually in the computer!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10947              "To tell you the truth, I never believed it-until now, of course."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10948              "Jet, this place is infested with horribly disfigured programs! I'd better hide!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10949              "Share this message with the Kernel."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10950              "Yes, sir. Go ahead."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10951              "Kernel, we are currently holding position near the perimeter of the server's internal partition. Rector scripts heavily populated the approach and we lost numerous command posts-next line."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10952              "The server appears to have a set of controller programs that prevent the virus from completely destroying all operating systems. Quite ingenious, actually-next line."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10953              "The controller programs protect the system memory, making it impenetrable-next line."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10954              "Awaiting your instructions-End of line."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10955              "I'll make sure the Kernel receives this right away, sir."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10961              "Are you safe?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10962              "For the time being. fCon sent me into the heart of Thorne's corrupted server. I'm sure they intended it as irony."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10963              "How are we going to get out of here? I think I'm on the same server."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10964              "Yes, of course. I had Mercury configure your routing instructions to find more information on Thorne. That must've led you here."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10965              "Why?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10966              "We need Ma3a and the correction algorithms to return home. I'm betting Thorne knows where she is."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10967              "Ma3a's insane! She tried to destroy me after compiling with the Legacy code!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10968              "That is a problem, but we need ...  "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10969              "They've found me ... "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10970              "Hang on, pop. I'm coming to help you."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10982              "Sir, the Controller Routines have been destroyed."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10983              "Good work."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10984              "Sir, we didn't do it."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10985              "A trap?-or was it just a computational glitch in our favor?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10986              "It doesn't matter. Primary instructions stand. Shields, take point! Group two, six, and twelve, flank left! Installers, prepare for launch! We're going in!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10987              "Our work is not done here until this system is clean! "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10988              "Tech, what's Alan's condition?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10989              "I'm seeing a lot of routing movement, but I haven't detected any errors. I'd say the process works perfectly."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10990              "Splendid! "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10991              "We're good to go, Mr. Crown?"
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10992              "Sir, the offsets are viable."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_10993              "Prepare the DataWraiths."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11000              "Dad, where are you? I've managed to access the server's internal partition."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11001              "Never mind that. We have another problem. What I'm guessing to be the network's Intrusion Countermeasure Programs are making their final assault on the corruption."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11002              "When I destroyed the Controller Routines, they stormed the partition."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11003              "Thorne is the only one that can lead us to Ma3a. We need to find him before they do."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11004              "My comrades ... "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11005              "Are you okay?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11006              "It was terrible-Crom, Codewall ... LAN ... all gone. "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11007              "Do you know how to reach the source of the corruption--how to reach Thorne?"
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11009              "The Kernel has uncovered a massive data stream that connects directly to the core. It will be over soon."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11010              "You've been a real pain in my side, Thorne."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11011              "Look at you. You're weak and pitiful. It's time to put an end to your reign of corruption."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11012              "Kernel, wait!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11013              "What is this?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11015              "Ugh! My back!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11016              "Maybe you better let me handle this, Dad."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11017              "You're a formidable opponent."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11018              "I knew I should have derezzed you when I had the chance."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11019              "Discs only program!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11020              " ... I'm so tired ... and ashamed."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11021              "fCon offered me a price I couldn't refuse. But it was my own greed that got me here. How was I to know the correction algorithms were real?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11022              "fCon's got Ma3a. They have the algorithms."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11023              "There's no stopping them now."
END

