STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11024              "You were part of the original plan. Where would they have taken Ma3a?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11025              "Their dedicated server, but it's impossible to penetrate. A massive firewall protects the only route in."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11026              "There must be some other way."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11027              "There is! A wireless dial-up that bypasses the firewall completely."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11028              "What's the number?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11029              "I never memorized it. It's stored on my PDA."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11030              "Would that work?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11031              "I don't see why not. Thorne, is your PDA connected to the network now?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11032              "Yes."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11033              "Hang on! If we can get the algorithms, maybe we can reverse the damage."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11034              "The Kernel was right. I'm weak and pathetic."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11037              "Let's find that data port and get out of here."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11038              "Dad? Dad?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11039              "What is the password?"
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11040              "Shoot! I should've asked Thorne for his password.  I don't ... "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11041              "That is not the password. Please go away."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11042              "OS, I need the dial up number to fCon's dedicated server."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11043              "Leave! I have important operations to attend to."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11044              "What happened to my father? We entered the port together."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11045              "I can only support one program at a time."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11055              "Okay! That's enough! I'll help you."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11056              "Make your way to the modem port and I'll activate the dial-up number."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11057              "You're not going to send me to some remote Russian satellite, are you?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11058              "It's tempting, but no. I just want you off of my system."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11059              "Here goes nothing ..."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11061              "Hey, what's this?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11062              "What happened? Are you okay?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11063              "Yes, I'm all right. I got bumped during the transfer. Are you in?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11064              "I'm in. Where are you?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11065              "I'm just outside the firewall. Thorne was right. There's no way past this thing."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11066              "I'll find a way. There's not a firewall anywhere I can't take down."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11067              "Oh yes, I nearly forgot about your alternative set of skills. Be careful, Jet."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11068              "Don't worry, Dad; it'll be a piece of cake."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11076              "What's happening? Why are they returning?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11077              "The system's fail-safe is kicking in. Something or someone is booting them off the server."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11078              "Get the doctor up immediately! We need to know what's going on."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11080              "Good work, Jet."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11081              "No sweat."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11082              "While I was waiting, I uncovered some interesting information about fCon."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11083              "They have plans to bring online a kind of mobile server that will allow them to shuttle their DataWraiths and stolen information over the Net. Once launched, their activities will be impossible to pinpoint."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11084              "We can't let them get away with this."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11085              "My feelings exactly."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11086              "Mr. Baza, I just lost Alan."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11087              "What do you mean, you lost him?"
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11088              "It looks like he entered our system, but I don't know how."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11089              "He knows too much. He could jeopardize the whole project."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11090              "Mr. Crown, perhaps it was foolish of you to send him in, no?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11091              "Tech, find him."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11092              "I'm working on it, sir."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11093              "Launch status is Alpha."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11094              "DataWraiths, begin preliminary boarding procedures. "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11095              "All data haulers and packet transports complete final routing tasks and return to storage partitions."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11096              "There's the server-Ma3a must be somewhere on board."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11097              "I need a peek at the server's schematics!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11098              "Jet, the schematic is going to take some time to decipher. In the mean time, make your way to the server's docking tethers."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11099              "What’s the status? This bird is launching in less than two hundred clock cycles."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11100              "Stabilizing bits are in place and balanced. Cross checking server stability ... now."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11101              "We need a smooth ride. Navigating the data port will be tricky. It'll be your base code if something goes wrong."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11102              "Yes sir! All computations will be executed correctly, sir!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11103              "According to the schematics, the transfer through the massive data port has very little room for error. Any instability in the server will cause it to crash."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11104              "That shouldn't be too hard. I've managed to crash many computers in my time."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11105              "Yes, it's simple from a User's point of view. It's a different story from in here."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11106              "You'll need to destroy the clamps securing the server's four primary stabilizing bits. Once onboard, we can send the command for the stabilizers to disengage."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11107              "And go down with the ship?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11108              "No, we'll need to find Ma3a and return home before the crash."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11109              "Sounds like it will be a close one."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11110              "At best."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11153              "Any progress?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11154              "All clamps are destroyed. This thing should go into a nice tailspin once launched."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11155              "Excellent! Meet me in the cargo bay sector. It's time to board the server and find Ma3a."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11156              "I think we have a problem."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11157              "What now?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11158              "DataWraith number A32 regained consciousness a few moments ago. He says there's a program, possibly a User, engaging our Wraiths."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11159              "Tech, is it Alan?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11160              "No, Mr. Crown."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11161              "Search Alan's lab server to see if someone snuck in when we weren't looking."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11162              "Sorry, we can't do that. That server has been completely reformatted. All data is gone."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11163              "Do your best to find out who else is in there."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11164              "Will do."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11165              "Launch status is Beta."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11166              "All DataWraith storage templates online."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11167              "Prepare for Release Candidate procession."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11168              "We've made it."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11169              "This far."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11176              "Where are they?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11177              "I thought I had one of them, but my Seeker Engine is no longer responding."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11178              "We need to take a firmer hand here, people."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11179              "Mr. Crown, prepare the team!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11180              "Yes, sir!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11181              "Hold on a minute ... I'm just here to wire this project up, not to participate. "
