STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11184              "Mr. Baza, think of all the zeros added to your Christmas bonus!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11185              "That, Mr. Crown, is music to my ears."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11186              "Tech, prepare the lasers."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11191              "Release Candidate has been approved. Launch status is Gold."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11192              "Onboard training grids activated."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11196              "What's our next move?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11197              "Find the Command Module and deactivate the stabilizer bits. I've got a lot of work to do here."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11198              "Ma3a doesn't look very happy to see us."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11199              "The TRON Legacy code was designed to exterminate Users in the system. In case of a contingency like this one."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11201              "I never would have suggested compiling the code if I knew you were in the system."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11217              "Dad, can you hear me?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11218              "Yes. Are you in trouble?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11219              "I think I've bitten off more than I can chew."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11220              "If I can just manage to decompile the TRON Legacy code from Ma3a, I may be able to restore an old friend of ours."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11221              "Do it quickly."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11222              "Hurry Dad! I don't know how much longer I can last."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11223              "There! I got it."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11224              "Mercury! Is it ... you?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11225              "It's me. Let's blow these guys to bits."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11226              "I managed to restore Mercury's settings as they were before she got caught in the reformat."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11232              "You've got to get off this server right away. In a few minutes it won't be safe for any program to be on."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11233              "You're leaving, aren't you? This is no world for a User. We are too crude and rudimentary."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11234              "If anybody is crude, it's us. We're not ready to exist here-not yet, anyway."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11235              "Promise you'll search for me."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11236              "Of course."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11239              "I guess this is end-of-line."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11242              "Tech, light this thing. We've got work to do."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11244              "Digitizing pads one, two and three online ... here we go ... "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11245              "Tech, what's going on?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11246              "The correction algorithms! They're gone"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11247              "Stop the procedure."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11248              "It's too late."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11252              "Warning! Operating system unstable."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11253              "System crash in thirty microcycles."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11254              "Normal shut down procedures failing. "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11255              "Permanent data loss reported in all sectors."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11256              "We have an unexpected visitor-or maybe I should say visitors."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11257              "More DataWraiths? Don't worry, Dad, I can take 'em."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11258              "No, something worse. I removed the correction algorithms from Ma3a to double check their integrity and ... well, something unpleasant happened."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11259              "Wonderful!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11260              "I'm reinstalling the correction algorithms now. By the time you make it back, we should be ready. But hurry! The ... creature hasn't noticed my presence yet."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11261              "The creature? Never mind, I'll be right there."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11262              "Jet, I'm activating the digitizing beam now!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11263              "Make sure you're right behind me!"
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11266              "Mercury!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11271              "Correction offset matrix cached and functioning correctly."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11272              "Ma3a what's happening? I'm receiving inconsistent output readings."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11273              "The corrupted User cluster entered the digitizing beam with Jet. Shall I complete the procedure?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11274              "No Ma3a."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11275              "They need to be removed from the current digitizing thread if we are to save them. "
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11276              "Understood, Alan One."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11277              "Do it quickly!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11278              "Jet, you must find a way to route the User cluster to the system's auxiliary memory storage or they will perish upon arriving into your analog environment."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11279              "Incapacitating their individual functions should make the task easier."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11280              "Output readings appear normal. Data transfer is complete."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11281              "Ma3a, bring my son home."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11282              "It's time, Jet. Alan One is waiting for you."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11283              "I've got to transfer Ma3a to my computer before the server crashes."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11284              "I'm encrypting her code so no one can get at her again."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11285              "What about Mercury? Is she off the system?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11286              "I don't show Mercury anywhere on the server-she's safe."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11287              "Just in time!"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11288              "We did it."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11289              "Yes, you certainly did. But you two will pay."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11290              "We'll deal with that later."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11291              "You haven't lost your touch either, Pop."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11292              "The fCon team-what'll happen to them?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11293              "I may be able to correct the mess they got themselves into-it'll take some time, but there's no hurry."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11294              "Hey, Dad ... you think I could get a copy of that Mercury program?  I need a good screensaver."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_11295              "Dad, to get to the Command Module, I must pass through a series of game grids."
END

