STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12001              "So you are a User ... Fascinating."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12003              "When a program has something to say, a talk icon will appear above his or her head."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12004              "To initiate the conversation, approach the program and press the action key."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12005              "Try it."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12009              "Tell me about player movement."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12010              "The basic player movements are forward, backward, strafe left, strafe right, crouch and jump. The mouse is used to look around.  You can also look around corners.  Here's a help file with more information."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12013              "That concludes the basics."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12015              "Tell me about my Status display."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12016              "The Status Display shows your Objectives and Tasks.  Press the Tab key to see an example."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12020              "Tell me about build points."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12021              "As you gain experience in the digital world, build points will be added to your version number.  At every milestone, you can use the build points to upgrade your performance ratings."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12022              "Here's a help file with more information."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12024              "Press the F1 key to access your performance ratings and distribute your initial set of build points."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12029              "Ma3a has just requested an I/O Node link with you."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12030              "You do not have the proper permission set to activate this object."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12031              "Tell me about I/O nodes."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12032              "I/O nodes are how programs communicate when not in the vicinity of each other."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12033              "I/O nodes, like most objects, require a permission set to activate. The segmented ring surrounding the reticle will indicate what permissions are missing."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12034              "To activate an object such as this I/O node, face the object and press the action key."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12035              "I believe that's it."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12038              "Looks like you don't have the proper permission set to access this archive bin, either."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12039              "Wait, I've got it here somewhere ... here you go."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12040              "Now that you have the proper permission set, activate the archive bin."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12041              "To download an item from an archive bin, select the corresponding number on your keyboard."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12042              "Tell me about archive bins."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12043              "Archive bins can contain permissions, emails, help files and subroutines."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12044              "Like most objects, they require a permission set to activate."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12045              "To activate, face the archive bin and press the action key."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12046              "One useful note. An empty archive bin exhibits no item nodes."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12047              "That about covers it."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12049              "To activate, face the I/O Node then press the action key."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12050              "Handling a disc is tricky. I strongly suggest a quick combat tutorial."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12051              "Ma3a has prepared a practice arena for you. The data stream leading to the arena is on the other side of this force field."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12052              "Unfortunately, the binary bit operating this socket is missing."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12053              "Lucky for us the missing bit is right here.  How about that?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12054              "Tell me about energy transfer."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12055              "Periodically, binary bits lack energy to operate properly."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12057              "To transfer energy to a bit, face the bit, then press and hold the action key. When the meter displayed in the HUD fills up, the transfer is complete."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12062              "Tell me about binary bits."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12063              "Binary bits are simple on and off switches."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12065              "To activate on object such as this binary bit, face the object and press the action key."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12068              "Now activate the bit to lower the force field."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12069              "To be transported to the combat training arena, step into the data stream."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12073              "Tell me about using the disc."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12074              "It's good practice to save your progress before entering into combat situations. Please do that now.  Step onto the battle ring when ready."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12075              "To throw the disc, click and release the left mouse button.  To recall the disc, click the right mouse button.  To steer the disc in mid-flight, click and hold the left mouse button.  Moving the mouse will influence the path of the disc."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12078              "To use the disc as a melee weapon, click the left mouse button while holding down the Control key."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12079              "To block an incoming enemy disc, press the right mouse button."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12080              "Practice using the disc against this combat training program."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12097              "Something's gone horribly wrong!  ROMie failed to transmit a data packet to my User.  He must have been corrupted!   He was so young, so many cycles left."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12099              "Let's go User, jump onto the ledge."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12100              "In the next sector there is an archive bin that contains a subroutine that will enable you to jump higher."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12101              "Locate the archive bin and retrieve the subroutine stored inside."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12110              "Greetings program! My name is ROMie. Please free me, I have an important packet to deliver."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12111              "Thanks, program."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12112              "Subroutines augment a program's base abilities when loaded into System Memory.  To load a subroutine, press the F1 key to bring up the menu and right click on the subroutine in the outer ring.  With the Y-amp loaded, your jump height is greater."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12113              "Thanks, program.  I was afraid my subroutines were going to become infected."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12115              "Follow me to the exit."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12117              "Strange little creature. What are they?"
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12118              "That is a Code Optimization Ware."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12120              "They graze on excess code. Activating one allows you to optimize a subroutine up one level."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12121              "To use, face the creature and activate."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12122              "Use wisely. They're only good for one optimization."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12125              "There's a sub-system that runs beneath the main level. Look down there."
END

STRINGTABLE DISCARDABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12135              "The corruption is spreading. We must keep moving."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12142              "Now this is unexpected.  These programs believe you are the source of the corruption. That's rather funny, actually."
    IDS_DIALOGUE_12143              "Come, you are not safe here.  We must find the server's exit port."
END

